# Cursor AI Rules for PlasmaVulkan Project

## Project Context
This is a Vulkan 1.4 volumetric particle rendering project using modern C++20.

## Code Style
- Use modern C++20 features
- Prefer RAII for resource management
- Use descriptive variable names
- Follow existing code patterns in the project

## Vulkan Specifics
- Always check VkResult return values
- Use VMA for memory allocation
- Prefer dynamic rendering over render passes
- Use compute shaders for particle physics

## Key Files
- src/renderer/VulkanContext.cpp - Core Vulkan setup
- src/core/Application.cpp - Main application loop
- shaders/*.comp - Compute shaders for particle simulation
- shaders/*.vert/frag - Rendering shaders

## Build System
- CMake with vcpkg for dependencies
- Visual Studio 2022 compiler on Windows
- Build directory: cmake-build-debug-visual-studio

## Common Commands
- Build: cmake --build cmake-build-debug-visual-studio --target PlasmaVulkan
- Run: ./cmake-build-debug-visual-studio/Debug/PlasmaVulkan.exe
- Compile shaders: cmake --build cmake-build-debug-visual-studio --target shaders

## Dependencies
- Vulkan 1.4
- GLFW for windowing
- GLM for math
- VMA for memory management
- volk for function loading